// @expect: true
// Pins UPSTREAM's pi, which gopherbuzz adopted on 2026-08-11.
//
// This file used to assert the opposite. It pinned the full-precision result and
// said "DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE, do not fix by adopting upstream's constant",
// because correct arithmetic was judged to beat bug-for-bug parity. That was
// reversed deliberately: this VM's job is to BE buzz, so a program moved from
// upstream must not get different numbers here.
//
// Its role is unchanged - catch a SILENT drift. It now fails if anyone quietly
// swaps buzzPi back to Go's math.Pi, which would give 114.59155902616465 and
// 3.141592653589793. See the note on buzzPi in std/math.go before changing either.
import "math";
final __r = math.deg(2.0) == 114.59155902616439
    and math.pi == 3.1415926535898
    and math.rad(math.deg(2.0)) == 2;
